Oh, I don't know. Nethack would have to change a lot of things to
become enticing enough to play it again, for me.

That the endgame is mostly boring is just the underwater part of
the iceberg. Now that I've seen a better way to handle them,
gods, alignment, skills, artifacts, resistances, bones, weapon
identification, shops, and probably some other things keep me
away, too (Re other thread; targetting anyone?).

Ever wanted to fight your own weapon? Or have your god take away
that pesky teleportitis, or half your current hitpoints/protect
you from harm/heal you without prompting, drop various scrolls
(some even useful), money, strawberries, armour you can't wear?

And for some reason, I can't help picturing Raisse as a follower
of Elyvilon (Crawl's healer god), there's hardly anything more
anti-evil (the other two 'good' ones are more warrior/priest-
like).

